fix: cope with a mount that passes no config object

The harness's own plugin tests mount with
`ctx.plugin({ name, inject, apply })`, which carries no `Config` for Cordis to
resolve — so `apply` received `undefined` and threw on the first property read.
A bundle-patch loader mounts the module namespace instead, Cordis fills the
schema defaults, and that path was already fine; only the object form failed.

`apply` now defaults its second parameter, which is also what the sibling
@argszero plugin does. Both spellings are pinned by a new test, the installed
probe exercises both, and the mutation that removes the default turns the suite
red (16/16 mutations, 20/20 tests).
